00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:53.316
"Space Pirate Captain Harlock
and his 40 crew members."

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.402
Wanted dead or alive.

00:03:55.652 --> 00:03:58.363
Reward is a full year's supply
of the finest quality energy capsules.

00:03:58.655 --> 00:04:00.198
Contact Mecha Police,
Megalopolis Station.

00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:39.488
"Galaxy Express Travel Center"

00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:48.538
They can't afford tickets.

00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:49.873
How pathetic!

00:04:57.839 --> 00:05:01.802
Unlimited access pass please,
including all local lines.

00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:07.641
Yes, including access
to the 999 train.

00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:32.749
I'll have that!

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.000
Thief?!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.085
Let's get him.

00:05:35.794 --> 00:05:37.087
Hey, catch!

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.952
You are under arrest,
for assault and robbery.

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:17.127
Damn it, let me go!

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.837
- Get your hands off!
- Be quiet.

00:06:37.772 --> 00:06:39.149
Mo...

00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:42.652
Mother?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:57.208
After him!

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.055
Here!

00:07:11.181 --> 00:07:13.850
All right, let's fly!

00:09:31.488 --> 00:09:32.864
Give me my...

00:09:32.864 --> 00:09:33.948
Pendant back...

00:09:35.909 --> 00:09:37.494
Don't let him get away!

00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:38.578
Kill him if necessary!

00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:49.732
It looks as though the last ship
has reached Megalopolis Station.

00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:53.695
Oh, it's starting to snow again.

00:10:53.695 --> 00:10:55.238
Brr, it's so cold!

00:10:59.284 --> 00:11:03.121
If we had Mechanized bodies,
we'd hardly feel the cold at all.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:09.085
Do people with Mechanized
bodies live a long time?

00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:10.753
Yes.

00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:13.506
As long as you take care
to replace worn parts...

00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:14.799
You could live forever,
they say.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:16.801
Forever?

00:11:21.181 --> 00:11:23.057
If only your father
were still alive...

00:11:23.057 --> 00:11:26.019
We could've gotten you
a Mechanized body.

00:11:34.485 --> 00:11:37.780
Then we gotta go to Megalopolis
and get on board the 999.

00:11:38.615 --> 00:11:41.868
Tickets cost an awful
lot of money, you know.

00:11:42.452 --> 00:11:45.079
| know, so I'll work hard!

00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.081
Then we can get on the 999
and go to the planet...

00:11:47.081 --> 00:11:50.084
That gives out mechanical
bodies for free.

00:11:52.712 --> 00:11:54.297
My, Tetsuro!

00:11:54.923 --> 00:11:56.382
You have it all worked out.

00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:57.926
Of course!

00:11:58.301 --> 00:11:59.677
I've got a really big dream.

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:00.970
Soc'm
on!

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:01.846
Let's hurry!

00:12:21.616 --> 00:12:22.825
Tetsuro, duck!

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:24.452
Trophy hunters!

00:12:57.151 --> 00:12:57.860
Mother!

00:12:58.778 --> 00:13:03.032
Count Mecha's hunters
kill humans for sport.

00:13:03.032 --> 00:13:04.033
Human hunters?

00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:13.751
We must've stumbled onto
Count Mecha's hunting grounds.

00:13:14.294 --> 00:13:17.505
Here, humans are nothing more
than trophies for the hunt...

00:13:19.215 --> 00:13:21.759
Mother, hang in there!

00:13:24.929 --> 00:13:25.930
I.oo

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.098
| can't.

00:13:27.557 --> 00:13:29.809
Please hurry, run away.

00:13:30.601 --> 00:13:31.185
No!

00:13:31.602 --> 00:13:32.603
I'm not going without you!

00:13:39.485 --> 00:13:42.030
You'll be on your
own now, Tetsuro.

00:13:42.905 --> 00:13:46.200
But I have faith in you.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.702
You're a strong boy...

00:13:47.702 --> 00:13:50.288
If you work hard,
you'll get that Mechanized body...

00:14:03.885 --> 00:14:07.180
Mother!

00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:13.061
| know it's here somewhere.

00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:14.479
Over there, my lord!

00:14:30.286 --> 00:14:32.163
Wonderful...

00:14:32.538 --> 00:14:34.707
I've never seen a
human this beautiful.

00:14:34.999 --> 00:14:36.334
What a lovely kill!

00:14:36.834 --> 00:14:38.920
I'll hang her on my wall.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:41.381
She will make a fine
addition to my collection.

00:14:44.592 --> 00:14:46.928
Back to the Time Castle.

00:14:46.928 --> 00:14:48.137
We'll raise a toast!

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:51.682
Time Castle?

00:15:15.665 --> 00:15:17.250
Mother!

00:15:24.882 --> 00:15:26.092
Damn them...

00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:28.845
Damn them...

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:34.684
Damn them!

00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:47.071
Wheream I?

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.250
Whoa!

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.668
It's Megalopolis!

00:16:05.756 --> 00:16:08.301
He's still sleeping.

00:16:10.303 --> 00:16:17.185
Listen Maetel, no matter what,
do not to leave that boy's side.

00:16:17.185 --> 00:16:21.314
Follow him like a shadow,
stay by his side to the very end.

00:16:21.689 --> 00:16:23.858
The more secrecy you
can maintain, the better.

00:16:23.858 --> 00:16:26.444
That is your mission, Maetel.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.529
| understand.

00:16:30.031 --> 00:16:31.324
"That boy?"

00:16:31.699 --> 00:16:32.909
Are they talking about me?

00:16:45.755 --> 00:16:46.422
Mother?

00:16:47.089 --> 00:16:48.841
Is something wrong?

00:16:48.841 --> 00:16:50.051
Uh, not at all!

00:16:50.301 --> 00:16:53.054
| just heard you
talking and thought...

00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:05.608
At least I thoughtl heard
you talking to someone...

00:17:09.862 --> 00:17:12.573
Anyway, who is she?

00:17:13.074 --> 00:17:17.078
She still looks human,
and so much like my mother!

00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:19.580
What are you talking
to yourself about?

00:17:22.041 --> 00:17:24.335
Oh, I was just dreaming
about my mother.

00:17:25.211 --> 00:17:25.753
Dreaming?

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.339
That's thanks
to the Dream Sensor.

00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:30.508
Using this...

00:17:31.467 --> 00:17:34.303
It's as if you're right there
in someone else's dream.

00:17:35.596 --> 00:17:37.139
Were you watching mine?

00:17:42.562 --> 00:17:43.604
So who are you?

00:17:44.021 --> 00:17:45.856
My name is Maetel.

00:17:46.232 --> 00:17:46.983
Maetel?

00:17:50.194 --> 00:17:53.406
If it wasn't for me, you'd be
at police headquarters now.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.212
You probably won't believe me,
but I'm not just some thief.

00:18:11.424 --> 00:18:12.258
But...

00:18:14.969 --> 00:18:17.471
You just need to be
on board the 999?

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:25.021
|I want to get a
Mechanized body.

00:18:25.855 --> 00:18:27.690
And what will you do
once you have it?

00:18:28.649 --> 00:18:30.526
| will kill Count Mecha!

00:18:41.829 --> 00:18:43.414
Shall I give you a pass?

00:18:44.915 --> 00:18:47.293
Or should I give this
back to you first?

00:18:51.922 --> 00:18:52.715
Mother!

00:18:53.507 --> 00:18:55.843
She still means that
much to you then?

00:18:56.719 --> 00:18:57.803
Of course she does!

00:18:58.262 --> 00:19:00.598
You have a mother too, right?

00:19:00.598 --> 00:19:02.892
| shouldn't have to
tell you how I feel--

00:19:06.228 --> 00:19:08.272
Or, is your mother...

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:15.613
| see...

00:19:16.113 --> 00:19:17.990
It's just that,
when I first saw you...

00:19:18.032 --> 00:19:21.285
You looked so much like
my mother that I got confused!

00:19:30.753 --> 00:19:33.005
Did you mean it, about the 999 pass?

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:35.591
You shouldn't tease me like that...

00:19:36.467 --> 00:19:39.970
Getting a Mechanized body
and killing Count Mecha...

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.389
Are those your only reasons
for boarding the 999?

00:19:42.014 --> 00:19:45.142
You've heard of Captain Harlock
and Emeraldas, haven't you?

00:19:49.814 --> 00:19:53.818
| wanna be like them,
sailing the Seas of Freedom!

00:19:54.819 --> 00:19:57.071
| wanna get a Mechanized
body and live on forever...

00:19:58.072 --> 00:19:59.824
Exploring the Sea of Stars.

00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:03.494
Isn't that what being
a man's all about?

00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:06.956
Harlock, Emeraldas.

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:09.542
They've become such
heroes to the young.

00:20:16.132 --> 00:20:16.757
Here.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:19.802
It's the real thing.

00:20:21.721 --> 00:20:24.014
| can really have it?

00:20:24.557 --> 00:20:25.474
On one condition.

00:20:25.891 --> 00:20:26.559
What's that?

00:20:27.685 --> 00:20:31.188
You'll have to go to the Andromeda
galaxy for a free Mechanized body.

00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:35.192
You can have the pass
if you let me accompany you.

00:20:35.609 --> 00:20:37.027
That is my condition.

00:20:38.154 --> 00:20:40.781
No problem, ladies shouldn't
have to travel alone anyway!

00:20:41.073 --> 00:20:42.867
- So, do we have a deal?
- Sure!

00:20:43.909 --> 00:20:44.702
I'm glad!

00:20:45.327 --> 00:20:47.997
Don't forget to sign it.

00:20:47.997 --> 00:20:50.583
It's not officially your
pass until you do.

00:20:53.002 --> 00:20:54.795
Go on, write your name.

00:20:58.674 --> 00:21:00.468
"Hoshino Tetsuro.”
(Iron Son of the Star Fields)

00:21:01.218 --> 00:21:02.762
What a manly name.

00:21:02.762 --> 00:21:03.345
Yes.

00:21:03.971 --> 00:21:05.014
My father gave it to me.

00:21:05.431 --> 00:21:07.016
Of course, your father.

00:21:10.978 --> 00:21:14.440
With this, I can finally board the 999.

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:22.031
I wouldn't care if Maetel was
a witch, or Death herself!

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:25.284
So long as I can take the 999
and get my mechanical body...

00:21:25.785 --> 00:21:26.535
I'll do anything!

00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:32.541
Open up!

00:21:33.042 --> 00:21:35.503
We know you're harboring
a fugitive human!

00:21:35.753 --> 00:21:36.962
We're onto you!

00:21:40.299 --> 00:21:41.634
Listen carefully, Tetsuro.

00:21:42.176 --> 00:21:45.679
Once you board the 999,
you can't ever come back to Earth.

00:21:47.348 --> 00:21:48.974
Either you'll make it
to Andromeda...

00:21:49.517 --> 00:21:51.936
Or you'll get off
on some backwater planet...

00:21:51.936 --> 00:21:53.354
Where you'll spend
the rest of your life.

00:21:53.979 --> 00:21:56.148
It'll all be up to fate.

00:21:58.609 --> 00:22:00.069
Are you sure you
won't regret this?

00:22:00.069 --> 00:22:01.028
Not a chance!

00:22:01.403 --> 00:22:03.322
All I care about
is getting on board the 999.

00:22:26.345 --> 00:22:28.764
Attention, please.

00:22:28.764 --> 00:22:35.354
Passengers for the 999,
departing at midnight...

00:22:35.354 --> 00:22:38.983
Bound for Andromeda,
please proceed to track 99

00:23:05.426 --> 00:23:06.010
Huh?

00:23:06.552 --> 00:23:08.679
This is the famous 999?

00:23:09.513 --> 00:23:11.348
Yes, does it surprise you?

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:15.644
| guess I wasn't expecting
such an old train...

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:16.812
Don't worry.

00:23:17.438 --> 00:23:20.232
It's actually a super-modern
space locomotive...

00:23:20.232 --> 00:23:22.443
Protected by an anti-energy infinite
source electro-magnetic barrier.

00:23:23.485 --> 00:23:28.365
It's only made up to look like
a relic from the distant past.

00:23:38.834 --> 00:23:40.377
Feel better now?

00:23:51.388 --> 00:23:53.474
Since many passengers
will never be coming back...

00:23:53.849 --> 00:23:56.644
The 999 was designed to give
them memories of simpler times.

00:24:00.314 --> 00:24:03.400
It might be as a machine,
but I'll be coming back!

00:24:12.368 --> 00:24:13.661
Today a boy...

00:24:14.328 --> 00:24:15.746
No, a young man...

00:24:15.746 --> 00:24:18.540
Has embarked on
the journey of his life.

00:24:19.249 --> 00:24:21.126
Defeat is not an option.

00:24:22.419 --> 00:24:26.423
It's a journey he'll remember
for the rest of his life.

00:24:27.549 --> 00:24:32.137
Tetsuro, your journey
is only just beginning.

00:25:12.511 --> 00:25:13.262
Finally...

00:25:14.013 --> 00:25:15.347
Finally, I'm leaving.

00:25:17.808 --> 00:25:18.851
Finally...

00:25:19.226 --> 00:25:19.893
I'm...

00:25:20.728 --> 00:25:21.353
I'm off!

00:25:38.954 --> 00:25:44.752
You can hear the steam whistle
of tomorrow, can't you?

00:25:45.919 --> 00:25:51.800
Clench the ticket
of your sweaty dreams

00:25:52.718 --> 00:25:59.641
With all your might
kick behind the wilted earth

00:25:59.641 --> 00:26:07.149
And head toward the stars.
Now, fly away!

00:26:08.233 --> 00:26:13.197
I'm leaving, I'm flying
I'm taking after the unknown

00:26:14.448 --> 00:26:21.663
Find a new star!

00:26:21.663 --> 00:26:29.171
Taking Off, Taking Off

00:26:29.171 --> 00:26:34.218
Toward a future nobody goes to

00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:45.479
Youth overtakes the light
and continues to run

00:26:46.563 --> 00:26:52.861
<i>The brilliant darkness fills to
the brim and expands outward</i>

00:26:53.362 --> 00:27:00.285
There has to be something
waiting there for you

00:27:00.285 --> 00:27:07.793
At the disappearing edge
of this beautiful galaxy

00:27:08.877 --> 00:27:14.424
I'm leaving, I'm flying
I'm taking after the unknown

00:27:15.092 --> 00:27:22.224
Don't look back
at familiar yesterday

00:27:22.224 --> 00:27:29.690
Taking Off, Taking Off

00:27:29.690 --> 00:27:35.571
Toward a future nobody goes to

00:27:36.155 --> 00:27:42.870
Taking Off, Taking Off...

00:28:16.278 --> 00:28:18.655
Look well, while you can.

00:28:20.699 --> 00:28:24.620
The next time you see Earth,
it will be with Mechanized eyes.

00:28:27.539 --> 00:28:28.498
That's okay.

00:28:28.498 --> 00:28:29.416
I've seen enough.

00:28:29.791 --> 00:28:32.169
Someday, even your most
heartbreaking memories...

00:28:32.794 --> 00:28:34.713
Will seem precious to you.

00:28:35.547 --> 00:28:38.175
You'll wish you had looked
when you had the chance.

00:28:39.635 --> 00:28:42.262
There'll be plenty of time
for that when I'm old!

00:28:43.222 --> 00:28:45.807
Right now, I just want
that mechanical body.

00:28:46.391 --> 00:28:48.894
That'll help make
my dreams come true.

00:28:58.612 --> 00:29:00.906
Uh, the next stop is Titan.

00:29:01.573 --> 00:29:02.658
Titan.

00:29:04.076 --> 00:29:06.954
The layover will be
for 16 Earth days.

00:29:07.287 --> 00:29:08.538
Sixteen days...

00:29:09.122 --> 00:29:11.291
Did he just say 16 days?

00:29:11.291 --> 00:29:12.125
He did.

00:29:13.001 --> 00:29:13.585
That's right!

00:29:14.211 --> 00:29:16.755
After all, Titan is one
of Saturn's satellites.

00:29:16.755 --> 00:29:18.715
Next to Earth's moon...

00:29:18.715 --> 00:29:21.093
It's the second-largest
satellite in the galaxy.

00:29:21.093 --> 00:29:25.180
Because its radius is so large--
5,800 kilometers to be exact...

00:29:25.180 --> 00:29:27.099
It takes 16 Earth-days
to complete one revolution.

00:29:27.933 --> 00:29:32.938
The train stops at each station for
exactly as long as the local day lasts.

00:29:32.938 --> 00:29:35.440
Each planet varies, of course.
Some have ten-hour days...

00:29:35.482 --> 00:29:37.234
While others take fifty.

00:29:37.234 --> 00:29:38.485
Correct, ma'am.

00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:41.530
All planets revolve
at different speeds.

00:29:43.156 --> 00:29:46.785
You're free to explore the planet
while the train is stopped.

00:29:47.286 --> 00:29:50.622
Just make sure you get back
on the 999 with time to spare...

00:29:50.622 --> 00:29:52.332
Or you'll be left for dead.

00:29:52.332 --> 00:29:53.125
For dead?

00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:55.127
You'll be stranded without
a backward glance, yes sir.

00:29:56.086 --> 00:29:58.130
That's a little strict, isn't it?

00:29:58.130 --> 00:30:01.675
Perhaps, but the Galaxy Express
runs strictly by the book!

00:30:14.563 --> 00:30:17.190
Titan is one of the most beautiful
places in the solar system...

00:30:17.733 --> 00:30:19.234
It's also one of the most terrifying.

00:30:20.068 --> 00:30:24.239
Long ago, islands of liquid methane
floated in a sea of ammonia...

00:30:24.656 --> 00:30:28.910
It had a nature incomprehensible
to those coming from other planets.

00:30:29.411 --> 00:30:34.082
Many lives were lost
transforming it into...

00:30:34.624 --> 00:30:36.668
The green planet you see today.

00:30:36.668 --> 00:30:39.713
Satellite Titan

00:30:39.713 --> 00:30:39.755
Satellite Titan

00:30:39.755 --> 00:30:39.796
Satellite Titan

00:30:39.796 --> 00:30:39.838
Satellite Titan

00:30:39.838 --> 00:30:39.880
Satellite Titan

00:30:39.880 --> 00:30:39.921
Satellite Titan

00:30:39.921 --> 00:30:39.963
Satellite Titan

00:31:04.196 --> 00:31:07.115
Whoa, this is great!

00:31:21.171 --> 00:31:21.797
He...

00:31:21.797 --> 00:31:22.672
he's been killed!

00:31:27.052 --> 00:31:27.886
Maetell!

00:31:28.512 --> 00:31:29.638
Wait!

00:31:29.638 --> 00:31:31.723
Don't come after me, Tetsuro!

00:31:57.332 --> 00:31:59.251
Finally awake?

00:32:01.002 --> 00:32:01.962
Wheream I?

00:32:04.714 --> 00:32:06.174
You're in my house.

00:32:08.051 --> 00:32:08.677
I.oo

00:32:08.677 --> 00:32:09.970
| want to know
where Maetel is!

00:32:10.429 --> 00:32:11.346
"Maetel?"

00:32:11.346 --> 00:32:13.765
Oh, you must mean
your traveling companion.

00:32:17.978 --> 00:32:21.106
She was kidnapped by
the bandits of Grape Valley.

00:32:21.106 --> 00:32:21.898
Bandits?

00:32:22.691 --> 00:32:24.943
Eat, before it gets cold.

00:32:31.992 --> 00:32:34.202
A man was killed
in front of the station.

00:32:35.120 --> 00:32:37.372
Maetel gets kidnapped
in broad daylight!

00:32:37.664 --> 00:32:39.499
What kind of a place
is this anyway?

00:32:39.499 --> 00:32:42.210
Titan is exactly what
it was created to be.

00:32:42.669 --> 00:32:48.300
A land where people can
do exactly as they please.

00:32:48.633 --> 00:32:51.386
That's the law of the planet,
the so-called Paradise Law.

00:32:51.386 --> 00:32:52.429
"Paradise Law?"

00:32:53.388 --> 00:32:55.307
What's going to
happen to Maetel?

00:32:57.017 --> 00:32:58.477
Where is Grape Valley?

00:32:58.894 --> 00:33:02.772
You'll only get yourself
killed going after her.

00:33:03.231 --> 00:33:07.903
When I got on the 999,
| promised I'd protect her.

00:33:08.403 --> 00:33:09.821
I've got to go after her!

00:33:10.280 --> 00:33:11.281
Where is this Grape Valley?

00:33:11.656 --> 00:33:12.491
Tell me where it is!

00:33:17.037 --> 00:33:19.831
There's a boat outside
at the end of the dock.

00:33:20.999 --> 00:33:22.834
It will take you down the river
and into Grape Valley.

00:33:22.834 --> 00:33:23.502
Thank you!

00:33:24.377 --> 00:33:25.086
Hold on!

00:33:34.346 --> 00:33:36.848
The sun's rays are stronger
than you'll be used to.

00:33:36.848 --> 00:33:39.476
Fainting in the middle
of a rescue won't do!

00:33:40.435 --> 00:33:43.313
You should take this too.

00:33:43.772 --> 00:33:45.065
What kind of gun is this?

00:33:45.607 --> 00:33:48.401
The kind that will protect you.

00:33:49.653 --> 00:33:51.238
But, it's such a great gun--

00:33:52.697 --> 00:33:54.324
You'd best hurry.

00:33:54.324 --> 00:33:56.910
It'll be dark before you know it.

00:34:08.088 --> 00:34:10.465
It may be a nice, warm planet...

00:34:10.465 --> 00:34:12.717
And it may be fine to do
whatever you want, but still...

00:34:12.717 --> 00:34:15.595
Living where it's okay to kill people
sure isn't what I'd call paradise!

00:34:18.640 --> 00:34:20.850
Somebody, help!

00:34:21.268 --> 00:34:23.603
Help!

00:34:27.899 --> 00:34:29.985
Help!

00:34:51.256 --> 00:34:52.090
You're safe.

00:34:52.674 --> 00:34:55.844
I've got you, you're safe.

00:35:24.956 --> 00:35:25.540
Boss!

00:35:25.665 --> 00:35:26.374
Boss!

00:35:26.791 --> 00:35:27.751
We heard a shot.

00:35:27.751 --> 00:35:29.210
Boss, you're bleeding!

00:35:29.210 --> 00:35:30.295
It's nothing.

00:35:30.295 --> 00:35:31.254
Just a scratch.

00:35:31.254 --> 00:35:32.255
Where's Maetel?!

00:35:33.298 --> 00:35:34.966
-Who's the kid?
- What the hell!

00:35:34.966 --> 00:35:36.092
Not so fast!

00:35:36.885 --> 00:35:38.803
This "kid" just saved her life.

00:35:46.353 --> 00:35:50.732
Tell me, kid, how'd you get
a Warrior's Weapon like that?

00:35:50.732 --> 00:35:51.900
A Warrior's Weapon?

00:35:52.484 --> 00:35:55.612
You're holding the only cosmo gun
capable of killing Mechanized men.

00:35:57.656 --> 00:36:00.742
The only one capable
of killing Mechanized men?

00:36:01.493 --> 00:36:02.118
This?

00:36:02.619 --> 00:36:04.621
Where did you get it!

00:36:05.288 --> 00:36:06.790
What business is that of yours?

00:36:07.457 --> 00:36:09.167
Just hurry up and hand over Maetel!

00:36:09.709 --> 00:36:12.170
Hey, kid, you can't talk
to our boss like that!

00:36:12.671 --> 00:36:16.549
Boss Antares is the most famous
bandit in Grape Valley!

00:36:16.549 --> 00:36:18.385
Show some respect, kid!

00:36:19.427 --> 00:36:20.595
What's your name?

00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:22.555
Stop calling me "kid" already!

00:36:22.889 --> 00:36:25.600
My name is Hoshino Tetsuro!

00:36:25.892 --> 00:36:27.060
How cute!

00:36:27.602 --> 00:36:29.854
This Maetel you're looking for...

00:36:29.854 --> 00:36:31.064
Are you in love with her?

00:36:31.356 --> 00:36:31.773
Huh?

00:36:32.357 --> 00:36:33.441
No, that's not--

00:36:33.983 --> 00:36:38.405
In exchange for a ticket on the 999,
| agreed to protect her.

00:36:38.405 --> 00:36:39.781
The 999...?

00:36:40.115 --> 00:36:43.201
So, you're after one of those
damned machine bodies, eh?

00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:45.036
How else am I gonna
kill Count Mecha!

00:36:45.328 --> 00:36:46.371
What's that?

00:36:46.621 --> 00:36:48.081
I'm gonna avenge my mother!

00:36:48.081 --> 00:36:48.957
Come with us.

00:36:48.957 --> 00:36:49.749
Ouch! Ouch!

00:36:49.749 --> 00:36:52.085
Hey, where are you taking me?

00:36:52.585 --> 00:36:54.504
Damn it, let me go!

00:36:54.504 --> 00:36:55.922
Let go!

00:38:00.445 --> 00:38:03.698
Once we put you through this,
we'll know if you're human or not.

00:38:03.948 --> 00:38:07.285
We'll see if you're really a
Mechanized man sent to kill me...

00:38:15.502 --> 00:38:17.128
So that's how it is...

00:38:17.128 --> 00:38:19.005
you're the real deal!

00:38:19.005 --> 00:38:22.717
A genuine human,
in the flesh no less!

00:38:26.179 --> 00:38:27.013
Maetel!

00:38:27.722 --> 00:38:28.306
Tetsuro!

00:38:30.475 --> 00:38:34.145
If you turn out to be a machine,
we'll disassemble you on the spot!

00:38:52.914 --> 00:38:54.999
Oh, my mistake!

00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:56.584
Sorry to embarrass you...

00:38:56.584 --> 00:38:58.878
You're definitely still human.

00:38:59.295 --> 00:39:01.422
An incredible specimen, at that!

00:39:01.422 --> 00:39:02.966
Please, forgive me.

00:39:05.718 --> 00:39:08.221
How's about I prove
myself to you, too?

00:39:13.309 --> 00:39:14.477
Wh-What are these?

00:39:14.936 --> 00:39:18.273
Souvenirs from my past...

00:39:18.606 --> 00:39:21.442
Unexploded shells picked up
during raids on various planets.

00:39:21.943 --> 00:39:24.070
Aren't you worried
they might go off?

00:39:24.529 --> 00:39:27.991
Nah, I figure I'll be gone
before I have time to worry.

00:39:44.382 --> 00:39:46.426
This is where the children live.

00:39:46.426 --> 00:39:47.677
It's a children's paradise.

00:39:48.219 --> 00:39:49.971
A children's paradise?

00:39:51.014 --> 00:39:52.181
Where are their parents?

00:39:52.181 --> 00:39:53.308
They're all orphans.

00:39:53.892 --> 00:39:54.642
Orphans?

00:39:55.101 --> 00:39:55.768
That's right.

00:39:55.768 --> 00:39:58.813
Like your mother, all their folks
were slaughtered by Count Mecha.

00:40:02.859 --> 00:40:05.111
Have you given any thought
as to how you'll find him?

00:40:05.862 --> 00:40:07.655
All I know is that
he's at the Time Castle.

00:40:09.240 --> 00:40:11.743
The location of which
remains a mystery to all...

00:40:12.076 --> 00:40:16.915
Except for the one person
who knows and isn't telling.

00:40:16.915 --> 00:40:17.790
Who's that?

00:40:18.124 --> 00:40:19.918
The female pirate Emeraldas.

00:40:20.251 --> 00:40:21.461
Emeraldas?

00:40:22.086 --> 00:40:24.088
No woman is more terrifying...

00:40:24.339 --> 00:40:29.677
One wrong word,
and off comes your head!

00:40:29.969 --> 00:40:32.388
So how can I find
this Emeraldas?

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:39.604
Don't worry, if she wants
you to find her, you will.

00:40:46.194 --> 00:40:47.111
Good stuff?

00:40:47.862 --> 00:40:49.405
Here's one last piece of advice:

00:40:49.864 --> 00:40:53.159
If you do ever find Count Mecha,
shoot before you get shot yourself.

00:40:54.786 --> 00:40:58.164
Even if he begs,
show him no mercy!

00:40:58.414 --> 00:41:01.542
Pause for even a moment,
and you're as good as dead.

00:41:02.377 --> 00:41:05.380
That's the galaxy's
first rule of survival.

00:41:10.802 --> 00:41:11.636
You take care.

00:41:12.345 --> 00:41:13.304
You too.

00:41:25.525 --> 00:41:28.277
So, you made it
back alive after all.

00:41:29.654 --> 00:41:30.488
Thank you.

00:41:30.905 --> 00:41:32.573
This gun saved my life.

00:41:32.573 --> 00:41:36.703
Why don't you hang
on to it a little longer?

00:41:36.703 --> 00:41:38.121
You may need it.

00:41:38.121 --> 00:41:40.039
But I heard this was
a Warrior's Weapon...

00:41:40.790 --> 00:41:42.875
It must be very
important to you.

00:41:43.251 --> 00:41:44.919
| want you to have it.

00:41:45.294 --> 00:41:46.087
Really?

00:41:46.087 --> 00:41:50.675
Those things belonged
to my only son, you see.

00:41:50.675 --> 00:41:57.724
That gun and hat went through
all kinds of danger with him.

00:41:58.558 --> 00:42:02.770
My son left them behind when
he went off to, wherever he went.

00:42:06.733 --> 00:42:10.236
When the time comes,
you should always return...

00:42:10.236 --> 00:42:13.114
To your mother and
father's side, one last time.

00:42:13.531 --> 00:42:15.491
Before they die, you know?

00:42:24.042 --> 00:42:25.460
Your son...

00:42:25.460 --> 00:42:26.961
what's his name?

00:42:27.837 --> 00:42:28.838
His name?

00:42:29.589 --> 00:42:32.925
Well, he'll be wearing the hat
| made for him, just like yours.

00:42:33.468 --> 00:42:35.553
If you should meet him
somewhere in the universe...

00:42:36.387 --> 00:42:37.221
If I do meet him...

00:42:37.764 --> 00:42:43.352
I'll tell him his mother
is still waiting for him.

00:42:43.603 --> 00:42:46.647
But I'm not fooling myself.

00:42:47.190 --> 00:42:51.402
| know he's not coming back.

00:42:51.611 --> 00:42:57.408
Still, when he wanted to leave
| knew I had no right to stop him...

00:42:58.076 --> 00:42:59.994
Sons all become men, after all.

00:43:00.495 --> 00:43:03.498
It's something we have to accept.

00:43:33.444 --> 00:43:34.612
The next stop...

00:43:34.612 --> 00:43:35.571
oh, dear...

00:43:36.489 --> 00:43:39.200
The next stop will be Pluto.

00:43:39.200 --> 00:43:40.576
That's Pluto, next stop.

00:43:46.374 --> 00:43:50.086
Please be advised the layover
will be for 6.39 days, that is all.

00:44:01.347 --> 00:44:02.807
So that's Pluto, huh?

00:44:03.266 --> 00:44:07.311
Experienced travellers
call it the "Faltering Planet."

00:44:08.354 --> 00:44:09.522
The Faltering Planet?

00:44:10.773 --> 00:44:15.486
Small and desolate,
it's a planet frozen to the core.

00:44:17.238 --> 00:44:19.365
No wonder it's so cold!

00:44:20.741 --> 00:44:24.036
Legend has it that
the cold is attributed...

00:44:24.036 --> 00:44:26.205
To the chill of the travelers
souls frozen there.

00:44:35.339 --> 00:44:37.675
Shhh, be still.

00:45:10.416 --> 00:45:14.754
When we were out in the snow,
my mother would warm me like this.

00:45:17.590 --> 00:45:21.135
It's almost like
she's alive again...

00:45:22.053 --> 00:45:22.678
Really?

00:45:55.378 --> 00:45:57.755
There's something I must do,
Tetsuro.

00:45:57.755 --> 00:45:58.923
You go ahead.

00:45:59.840 --> 00:46:04.387
Look around a bit if you like,
but stay within city limits.

00:46:04.845 --> 00:46:06.097
Hey, I've got a gun!

00:46:06.097 --> 00:46:06.722
I'll be fine.

00:46:07.515 --> 00:46:09.684
But a gun can't keep you warm!

00:47:23.174 --> 00:47:24.342
Wh-Who are you?

00:47:25.009 --> 00:47:26.510
My name is Shadow.

00:47:27.261 --> 00:47:29.430
| tend the graves of ice.

00:47:30.139 --> 00:47:31.474
Graves of ice?

00:47:34.435 --> 00:47:36.020
This is where those
who died of illness...

00:47:36.395 --> 00:47:42.068
Or who abandoned their humanity
for Mechanized bodies sleep eternally.

00:47:43.152 --> 00:47:45.112
Abandoned their humanity?

00:47:52.661 --> 00:47:53.579
Cold!

00:47:53.871 --> 00:47:57.708
Come with, me and I'll
show you my former self.

00:47:58.709 --> 00:48:04.173
While I could travel to many exotic
planets with my Mechanized body...

00:48:04.965 --> 00:48:07.301
| could never forget
my human form.

00:48:07.343 --> 00:48:11.222
Thus, I became caretaker
here to remain by its side.

00:48:12.390 --> 00:48:13.099
Let go of me!

00:48:13.474 --> 00:48:15.935
You're freezin' me, let go!

00:48:18.062 --> 00:48:19.522
Isn't she beautiful?

00:48:20.398 --> 00:48:21.982
That was me, long ago.

00:48:23.067 --> 00:48:25.820
| knew no machine
could be as beautiful.

00:48:27.154 --> 00:48:31.784
No face would be as satisfying,
so I chose not to have one at all.

00:48:32.785 --> 00:48:37.331
That's why everyone calls me
Shadow of the Faltering Planet.

00:48:39.375 --> 00:48:40.459
Lemme go!

00:48:40.459 --> 00:48:41.460
Let go, I said!

00:48:47.258 --> 00:48:47.883
Put me down!

00:48:48.092 --> 00:48:49.385
What do you want from me?

00:48:50.010 --> 00:48:53.305
Oh, I just want you to
stay here with me...

00:48:53.305 --> 00:48:54.181
forever.

00:48:54.181 --> 00:48:54.682
Forget it!

00:48:55.015 --> 00:48:56.225
Let go!

00:48:56.225 --> 00:48:57.893
Good night, little boy.

00:48:58.519 --> 00:48:59.478
Good night...

00:49:02.398 --> 00:49:03.649
Shadow, that's enough!

00:49:08.988 --> 00:49:09.655
Shadow!

00:49:10.448 --> 00:49:13.576
Becoming a machine
was your own choice.

00:49:14.618 --> 00:49:18.247
| know you must be lonely,
but taking his life isn't fair.

00:49:19.457 --> 00:49:22.334
It's not his fault you lack
the courage to choose...

00:49:22.334 --> 00:49:26.589
between a limited human life
or living forever as a machine!

00:49:26.589 --> 00:49:27.798
Stop it, Maetel!

00:49:35.598 --> 00:49:37.099
Ready to leave, Tetsuro?

00:49:53.491 --> 00:49:57.661
The human bodies
are kept here...

00:49:57.995 --> 00:50:00.206
So that those with Mechanized
bodies might return to them.

00:50:01.665 --> 00:50:04.043
Whether or not this
is really a kindness...

00:50:04.668 --> 00:50:07.880
Or an act of cruelty to those
who have forsaken their humanity...

00:50:08.756 --> 00:50:10.758
Has never been decided.

00:50:11.509 --> 00:50:15.471
Come on Maetel, you're talking like
you've got a Mechanized body yourself!

00:50:16.180 --> 00:50:19.058
Oh, Shadow just has that
effect on me, that's all.

00:50:48.504 --> 00:50:52.216
Who was Maetel looking at
in that icy grave?

00:50:53.551 --> 00:50:56.095
What sort of secrets
does she keep?

00:50:57.012 --> 00:50:57.846
That's right!

00:51:13.529 --> 00:51:15.990
Let's say I do find out
what's in Maete!'s past.

00:51:16.574 --> 00:51:17.825
Do I really need to know?

00:51:18.325 --> 00:51:20.536
Am I better off not knowing?!

00:51:27.376 --> 00:51:27.918
Not good!

00:51:57.239 --> 00:51:57.906
Something wrong?

00:51:58.616 --> 00:52:03.287
No, I'm just not used to
eating in fancy places like this.

00:52:04.663 --> 00:52:05.748
Welcome!

00:52:10.210 --> 00:52:11.295
Is that glass?

00:52:11.295 --> 00:52:12.796
Or acrylic, maybe...

00:52:12.796 --> 00:52:15.591
I'm actually made of lead glass.

00:52:16.467 --> 00:52:17.384
And your name?

00:52:17.384 --> 00:52:18.385
It's Claire.

00:52:18.385 --> 00:52:19.136
Thank you.

00:52:19.136 --> 00:52:20.095
Of course.

00:52:25.976 --> 00:52:28.312
Tetsuro, be sure to eat well.

00:52:29.938 --> 00:52:31.857
Let's see...

00:52:38.197 --> 00:52:39.448
Have you decided?

00:52:39.782 --> 00:52:40.157
Huh?

00:52:40.908 --> 00:52:42.785
Uh, well--

00:52:43.494 --> 00:52:45.829
Shall we have steak, Tetsuro?

00:52:46.288 --> 00:52:47.331
Yeah, good idea!

00:52:47.665 --> 00:52:48.540
Two steaks please.

00:52:48.832 --> 00:52:49.792
And how would you
like those done?

00:52:52.336 --> 00:52:55.339
Medium-rare, please,
with the corn soup.

00:52:55.714 --> 00:52:58.217
Bread with mine, he'll have rice.

00:52:58.217 --> 00:52:59.009
Sounds good.

00:52:59.009 --> 00:53:00.219
Very good.

00:53:05.516 --> 00:53:08.310
Shadow's body was kinda
see-through, too...

00:53:08.727 --> 00:53:10.562
But she was cold!

00:53:10.562 --> 00:53:11.563
Why is Claire warm?

00:53:12.106 --> 00:53:15.067
Maybe your feelings make
Claire seem warmer than she is.

00:53:15.067 --> 00:53:15.567
What!

00:53:16.360 --> 00:53:17.194
Come on...

00:53:18.320 --> 00:53:20.155
Is it too warm in here?

00:53:20.155 --> 00:53:21.824
Your face is so red!

00:53:21.824 --> 00:53:24.284
Oh, no, it's just, uh...

00:53:25.035 --> 00:53:29.998
Tetsuro seems fascinated
by your lead glass body.

00:53:29.998 --> 00:53:33.711
It was my mother--
who was very vain..

00:53:33.711 --> 00:53:35.295
That decided it should be glass.

00:53:36.755 --> 00:53:40.426
I'm working here to save enough
money to buy back my real body.

00:53:40.926 --> 00:53:44.722
It's being stored for me
on Pluto at the moment.

00:53:44.722 --> 00:53:47.182
You mean it's underneath
all that ice?

00:53:47.182 --> 00:53:47.766
Yes.

00:53:48.684 --> 00:53:51.979
Sometimes on my days off,
| go down to the surface of Pluto...

00:53:51.979 --> 00:53:53.897
Just to look at it a while.

00:53:54.857 --> 00:53:56.316
But this body's so pretty.

00:53:56.608 --> 00:53:57.401
Why thank you.

00:53:58.277 --> 00:54:00.320
But in this body made of glass...

00:54:01.864 --> 00:54:05.284
Both light and shadows
pass right through it.

00:54:05.701 --> 00:54:07.703
That makes me very
very sad sometimes.

00:54:17.129 --> 00:54:19.381
Your hand is so warm.

00:54:29.516 --> 00:54:30.726
What happened to the lights?

00:54:30.726 --> 00:54:32.144
We've entered a tunnel, is all.

00:54:32.311 --> 00:54:32.978
A tunnel?

00:54:33.228 --> 00:54:33.937
In space?

00:54:34.271 --> 00:54:37.775
It's a space tunnel through
the dimensional asteroid field.

00:54:38.358 --> 00:54:42.070
The train's electrical system
doesn't function inside the tunnel.

00:54:42.279 --> 00:54:43.697
The safety valves close.

00:54:46.658 --> 00:54:47.785
You're like a firefly!

00:54:47.785 --> 00:54:50.496
Doing this makes my body
just a little warmer.

00:54:59.129 --> 00:55:00.589
How was your steak, Tetsuro?

00:55:00.589 --> 00:55:01.590
It was great!

00:55:03.592 --> 00:55:05.052
I'll take care of the bill.

00:55:05.052 --> 00:55:06.553
Why don't you go back?

00:55:06.553 --> 00:55:08.222
I'll escort you.

00:55:21.193 --> 00:55:24.279
Thanks, I think I can
find my way from here.

00:55:24.696 --> 00:55:26.073
Sure, I'll just be--

00:55:30.410 --> 00:55:31.370
Another tunnel?

00:55:31.370 --> 00:55:33.121
We should be out of it by now.

00:55:36.542 --> 00:55:37.292
Conductor?

00:55:37.334 --> 00:55:37.751
Huh?

00:55:38.168 --> 00:55:38.794
Yes, what is it?

00:55:39.503 --> 00:55:41.213
What's going on out there?

00:55:41.213 --> 00:55:42.422
My apologies...

00:55:42.673 --> 00:55:45.259
There's an unidentified ship
flying parallel to us, it seems.

00:55:46.134 --> 00:55:46.969
A ship?

00:55:46.969 --> 00:55:47.803
You mean that?

00:55:48.220 --> 00:55:48.887
Yes, sir.

00:55:53.183 --> 00:55:53.934
Hey, that's--

00:56:03.277 --> 00:56:04.987
This is Emeraldas.

00:56:05.362 --> 00:56:07.364
I claim right of way.

00:56:07.489 --> 00:56:10.492
999, lower your
speed immediately

00:56:27.217 --> 00:56:28.176
Emeraldasl!

00:56:28.552 --> 00:56:30.262
| need to ask you something!

00:56:30.470 --> 00:56:32.139
Please, tell me!

00:56:33.223 --> 00:56:35.100
Wait, what is he doing?

00:56:47.029 --> 00:56:48.572
What have you done?!

00:57:54.137 --> 00:57:56.807
Which one of you
fired at my ship?

00:58:04.064 --> 00:58:05.983
One of you must have...

00:58:09.861 --> 00:58:10.946
Show yourself!

00:58:17.119 --> 00:58:17.995
It was me.

00:58:18.453 --> 00:58:19.162
It was you?

00:58:19.663 --> 00:58:20.998
Are you a bounty hunter?

00:58:23.041 --> 00:58:26.086
No man has ever pulled
a gun on me and lived!

00:58:41.685 --> 00:58:43.937
Only a foolish man puts
so little value to his life...

00:58:45.647 --> 00:58:47.441
And you're hardly a man yet!

00:58:56.116 --> 00:58:58.243
Where did you get this gun?

00:58:59.745 --> 00:59:00.787
On Titan.

00:59:00.787 --> 00:59:03.290
An old woman
gave it to me, along with a hat.

00:59:03.623 --> 00:59:04.458
A hat?

00:59:05.375 --> 00:59:06.293
This hat.

00:59:09.755 --> 00:59:10.756
Maetel...

00:59:16.678 --> 00:59:18.889
Do you have any idea...

00:59:18.889 --> 00:59:20.807
Where the original owner
of this hat and gun is?

00:59:29.733 --> 00:59:30.484
| see.

00:59:34.321 --> 00:59:35.822
How have you been, Maetel?

00:59:35.822 --> 00:59:37.407
| hadn't expected to find you here.

00:59:38.283 --> 00:59:40.452
I'm doing well, Emeraldas.

00:59:40.452 --> 00:59:43.955
Maetel, I didn't know
you knew Emeraldas!

00:59:43.997 --> 00:59:45.665
Why didn't you say something?

00:59:47.125 --> 00:59:49.377
Because I knew you'd find her,
even without my help.

00:59:49.878 --> 00:59:53.256
Emeraldas, Tetsuro has
a question for you.

00:59:54.007 --> 00:59:54.800
For me?

00:59:55.425 --> 00:59:57.469
| was told it's something
only you would know.

00:59:57.761 --> 01:00:00.347
Where will Count Mecha's
Time Castle appear next?

01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:01.723
Count Mecha?

01:00:02.265 --> 01:00:03.225
Please.

01:00:03.225 --> 01:00:04.935
If you know, tell him.

01:00:06.144 --> 01:00:07.312
Why do you want to know?

01:00:09.564 --> 01:00:12.567
You mean to kill him,
Count Mecha himself?

01:00:14.236 --> 01:00:15.278
You're serious!

01:00:15.278 --> 01:00:17.656
If you know, Emeraldas,
tell him.

01:00:19.783 --> 01:00:20.951
Are you sure?

01:00:22.077 --> 01:00:24.538
You really want me
to tell him?

01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:32.712
Count Mecha's
Time Castle...

01:00:37.384 --> 01:00:39.553
...will next appear at
Trader's Fork...

01:00:39.553 --> 01:00:41.596
Where a viewing of his collection
will be held for his associates.

01:00:42.222 --> 01:00:43.431
Trader's Fork?

01:00:44.307 --> 01:00:45.851
Trader's Fork is our
next stop, sir!

01:00:49.813 --> 01:00:51.565
"Tetsuro" wasn't it?

01:00:51.565 --> 01:00:54.818
You should value your
one and only life more.

01:00:59.239 --> 01:01:00.115
Emeraldas!

01:01:05.162 --> 01:01:06.037
Thank you.

01:01:27.142 --> 01:01:29.394
| suppose I should
thank you too, Maetel.

01:01:29.603 --> 01:01:30.562
Why me?

01:01:31.021 --> 01:01:35.650
If you weren't Emeraldas' friend,
I'd be a goner by now!

01:01:38.236 --> 01:01:39.070
Well, maybe!

01:01:40.447 --> 01:01:45.118
But Emeraldas is looking for the
owner of that gun and hat you have.

01:01:46.536 --> 01:01:48.997
So you're ea yin' that the old
woman's son is...

01:01:48.997 --> 01:01:51.499
Emeraldas' beloved.

01:01:51.499 --> 01:01:53.877
A man to whom she has given
her heart and life to.

01:02:00.342 --> 01:02:04.930
Conductor, couldn't we just
skip the stop at Trader's Fork?

01:02:06.348 --> 01:02:08.558
What are you saying, Claire?

01:02:08.558 --> 01:02:12.437
If the train doesn't run on time,
I'll be fired for negligence!

01:02:12.729 --> 01:02:15.232
But, if we stop there...

01:02:15.232 --> 01:02:17.859
Tetsuro will get himself killed
going after Count Mecha!

01:02:17.859 --> 01:02:20.946
So just this once, can't we pass
Trader's Fork without stopping?

01:02:23.740 --> 01:02:28.328
Tetsuro means a lot to you,
doesn't he Claire?

01:02:29.162 --> 01:02:31.039
No, of course not!

01:02:40.882 --> 01:02:42.717
Trader's Fork:

01:02:43.677 --> 01:02:45.345
The great way station
where all tracks in the universe meet.

01:02:45.345 --> 01:02:45.387
The great way station where all tracks in
the universe meet. Planet Heavy Melder

01:02:45.387 --> 01:02:45.428
The great way station where all tracks in
the universe meet. Planet Heavy Melder

01:02:45.428 --> 01:02:45.470
The great way station where all tracks in
